I think I've decided where I'm going to go with it.  And it's 
something of a "middle way."  I'll make something 'familiar' 
to nethackers, with a lot of features nethackers will recognize 
(pets, shops, amulet of Yendor, Rodney, Vlad's tower, Medusa, 
Fort Ludios, much of the item and monster lists, etc) but I've 
decided to treat it as a successor with its own identity, rather 
than a reimplementation effort attempting to recreate nethack's 
balance and game mechanics.  I'll not attempt to recreate 
"The Same Game" in detail.  I'll treat questions of balance and 
game mechanics as needing new answers, not as having answers that 
need copied from nethack. 

I'll skip things I think might be infringing.  I'll skip things 
that don't belong with the things that are there (anachronistic, 
Australian, Japanese, and Chinese elements should be in games 
with different settings).  I'll skip things that are too 
arbitrary or obscure (ie, useful only to the spoiled and make 
no sense anyway, like cursed scrolls of gold detection).  I'll 
skip things that in my opinion give the player too many options 
(like wishes). I'll fundamentally change some races/classes and 
eliminate others.  I'll add a lot of new and unfamiliar material, 
including some directly contradictory to the setting and background 
of nethack.  It'll be a different game. 

